alex 2.1.0 (Hackage tarball), built with mhs for ghc66/alex210ddc.nix. Every
change is under `#if defined(__MHS__)` or keeps the meaning of the code:

  Main.hs        Control.Exception's bracketOnError, in place of the local one
                 built on block/unblock, which MicroHs does not have
  Map.hs         a branch over the chain's Data.Map shim (common/shims), which
                 lacks unionWith, mapWithKey and fromListWith
  NFA.hs,        Functor and Applicative instances for the NFAM and P monads
  ParseMonad.hs  (superclasses of Monad in MicroHs's base)
  Output.hs      unsafeRead as readArray (the shim's Data.Array.Base has none;
                 its one use is on an array whose lower bound is 0), and
                 `paren.outputAcc` spaced to `paren . outputAcc`: MicroHs reads
                 `a.b` as a record field selection

The build also passes -D__GLASGOW_HASKELL__=604, so Map.hs and the generated
Scan.hs take the GHC >= 6.3 branches (Data.Map, Data.Array), and an empty
ghcconfig.h for the generated Scan.hs's #include.

